# Configuration template. Two ways to supply real credentials:
#
#   PREFERRED: keep keys in ONE private file outside every repo, e.g.
#   ~/.secrets/ai.env (chmod 600), and point ENV_FILE at it per run:
#       ENV_FILE=~/.secrets/ai.env BOUNDARY_PROVIDER=anthropic python scripts/real_run.py
#       ENV_FILE=~/.secrets/ai.env BOUNDARY_PROVIDER=openai    python scripts/real_run.py
#   scripts/run_demo.py is always the offline mock and reads no provider.
#   Keys never appear in commands, shell history, or the repository.
#
#   ALTERNATIVE: cp .env.example .env and fill it in. NEVER commit .env.
#
# With no provider configured the system runs the deterministic offline mock.

# mock | anthropic | openai
# A provider name without its matching key falls back to the mock, so the
# tests, the demo and the gate never depend on the network.
BOUNDARY_PROVIDER=mock

# Required only for the matching provider:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra

# HMAC key for pseudonymized redaction tokens.
#
# THE DEFAULT IS PUBLISHED AND IS NOT A SECRET. It is safe only because the
# shipped corpus is synthetic. A stable key is what makes a pseudonym linkable
# across requests, so anyone holding this key can confirm a guessed value by
# recomputing its token -- an SSN has an input space of 10^9 and an email
# address is a dictionary. Supply your own for anything that is not this demo,
# and see the salt note below for what rotating the tokens costs.
# BOUNDARY_PSEUDONYM_KEY=change-me
#
# Rotating the salt breaks cross-request linkage and also breaks the
# operational usability that motivated pseudonymization. The salt is applied
# to every token; choosing a rotation schedule is left to the deployment.
# BOUNDARY_PSEUDONYM_SALT=2026-08

# Where the hash-chained audit trail is written. Runtime artifact, gitignored.
# AUDIT_LOG_PATH=audit/boundary.audit.jsonl

# Embeddings are OpenAI-only. Anthropic publishes no embeddings endpoint, so
# BOUNDARY_PROVIDER=anthropic gives real completions and MOCK vectors, and
# scripts/real_run.py prints the two seams on separate lines for that reason.
# The embedding model is text-embedding-3-small at 1536 dimensions; see
# boundary/providers.py.
